¦ A riddle, an enigma, a conundrum.
 It is thus defined in the {#vidagDamuKamaRqana --vyaktIkftya kamapyarTaM#}
 {#svarUpArTasya gopanAt . yatra bAhyAntarAvarTO kaTyete sA prahelikA#}.
 It is {#ArTI#} or {#SAbdI#}; {#taruRyAliNgitaH kaRWe nitambasTalamASritaH .#}
 {#gurURAM sanniDAne'pi kaH kUjati muhurmuhuH#} (where the answer is {#IzadUnajalapUrRakumBaH#})
 is an instance of the former kind; {#sadArimaDyApi na vEriyuktA nitAntaraktApyasitEva#}
 {#nityam . yaToktavAdinyapi nEva dUtI kA nAma kAnteti nivedayASu ..#} (where
 the answer is {#sArikA#}), of the latter. Daṇḍin, however, mentions 16
 different kinds of {#prahelikA#}; see <ls>Kāv. 3. 96-124</ls>.
